# CODEOWNERS — Maintainer governance (inspired by openai/codex)
# https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Rule: patterns later in the file take precedence (last match wins).
#       Hence the catch-all * is at the top, specific paths below.
# With branch protection (require_code_owner_reviews):
#   a PR touching a path must be approved by its owner before merging.
#
# ⚠️ Currently falls back to the @ai007-explorer org. To split roles later:
#   maintainer = @someone   (final merge decision on source)
#   committer  = @someone,@someone (governance / CI / docs approval)
# Just replace @ai007-explorer below with concrete GitHub usernames.

# ── Default catch-all (anything not matched above → whole org) ───────────
*                                           @ai007-explorer

# ── Core source (recommend sole approval; replace @ai007-explorer with maintainer username)
/server.js                                   @ai007-explorer
/auth.js                                     @ai007-explorer
/projection-route.js                         @ai007-explorer
/gen_projection.py                           @ai007-explorer
/public/                                     @ai007-explorer

# ── Governance / CI / merge mechanism (changes need broader visibility) ──
/.github/CODEOWNERS                         @ai007-explorer
/.github/settings.yml                       @ai007-explorer
/.github/workflows/                         @ai007-explorer
/.github/                                   @ai007-explorer

# ── Docs / deployment config ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/README.md                                  @ai007-explorer
/railway.json                               @ai007-explorer
/projection.json                            @ai007-explorer
